---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import home from '../data/home.json';
const H: any = home;
const parts = Object.values(H).reduce((n: number, x: any) => n + x.parts, 0);
const papers = Object.values(H).reduce((n: number, x: any) => n + x.papers, 0);
---
<Base title="About this site" context="about" description="Who runs sciencegcsetutor.com and where the questions, mark schemes and ratings come from.">
  <h1>About this site</h1>
  <p>sciencegcsetutor.com is run by {site.company}, a tutoring business with a small team of specialist tutors. The site exists to give GCSE science students the past-paper material they actually use, sorted the way they revise, free and without sign-up; and to introduce students who want more help to a tutor who teaches science every week.</p>
  <h2>Where the material comes from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Questions, mark schemes and examiner comments</strong> are from AQA's own papers for every higher-tier series of GCSE Biology (8461), Chemistry (8462), Physics (8463) and Combined Science: Trilogy (8464) since the first exams in June 2018, plus AQA's specimen papers: {papers} papers and {parts.toLocaleString()} question parts. A few papers that AQA has since taken off its website are included from copies of AQA's own PDFs; the paper pages say which. Each part has been tagged to the specification statements it assesses, its maths and practical skills, any required practical, and its question type. Where a part needs a figure, table or graph printed in an earlier part of the question, that earlier part folds out above it.</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty ratings</strong> (Easy and Hard) come from AQA's examiners' reports: Easy where the report says most students scored the marks (60% or more), Hard where few did (under 35%). Parts the report gives no figure for are left unrated.</li>
    <li><strong>The notes on the required practicals, maths skills, the physics equations and the six-mark questions</strong> are the site's own writing, checked by our tutor; they are not copied from AQA's material.</li>
    <li><strong>Grade boundaries and exam dates</strong> are AQA's published figures.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who teaches</h2>
  <p>The tutoring is by Sam, a qualified teacher who currently teaches A-level Biology at an outstanding sixth-form college and taught GCSE Science for many years; see the <a href="/tutors/">tutor page</a>. The site is built and maintained by the same small team that runs <a href="https://www.alevelbiologytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelbiologytutor.com</a> and <a href="https://www.aleveltutors.online" rel="noopener">aleveltutors.online</a>.</p>
  <h2>Mistakes</h2>
  <p>If you find one, tell us on the <a href="/report/">report a mistake</a> page; corrections usually go live the same week.</p>
</Base>
